WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.633 --> 00:00:05.872
[music playing]

00:00:05.939 --> 00:00:08.908
NARRATOR: In Bimini,
Bahamas, a team of experts

00:00:08.975 --> 00:00:17.417
are hoping to entice a couple
sharks for an experiment

00:00:17.484 --> 00:00:20.787
and get more than
they bargained for.

00:00:20.854 --> 00:00:24.190
[music playing]

00:00:33.133 --> 00:00:36.102
They're testing if sharks
can detect magnetic fields.

00:00:38.938 --> 00:00:42.675
The answer could unlock a major
mystery about how sharks find

00:00:42.742 --> 00:00:46.179
far-flung, food-rich
volcanic islands

00:00:46.246 --> 00:00:48.815
and whether the island's
naturally magnetic lava

00:00:48.882 --> 00:00:49.582
rock is involved.

00:00:52.886 --> 00:00:55.655
For this open water
experiment, they

00:00:55.722 --> 00:00:58.758
arranged three powerful
magnets to the right

00:00:58.825 --> 00:01:01.528
and three non-magnetic
controls to the left.

00:01:10.403 --> 00:01:13.673
A big hammerhead glides
over the aluminum control

00:01:13.740 --> 00:01:16.209
without a glance and
heads for the magnets.

00:01:37.564 --> 00:01:43.670
Hammerheads ignore the aluminum,
clustering around the magnets.

00:01:43.736 --> 00:01:45.805
The nurse sharks have
a greater response.

00:02:06.593 --> 00:02:08.695
Nurse sharks are
drawn to the magnets.

00:03:06.219 --> 00:03:10.523
The sharks are agitated,
possibly by the magnets.

00:03:10.590 --> 00:03:13.893
[music playing]

00:03:25.138 --> 00:03:26.940
That was fantastic.

00:03:27.006 --> 00:03:28.274
That was great.

00:03:28.341 --> 00:03:31.244
So many hammerheads down
there, all over the place.

00:03:31.311 --> 00:03:32.378
A bunch of nurse sharks.

00:03:32.445 --> 00:03:34.447
The nurse sharks were
playing at the magnets.

00:03:34.514 --> 00:03:36.316
Really neat dive all around.

00:03:36.382 --> 00:03:38.384
Yeah so that dive was crazy.

00:03:38.451 --> 00:03:39.919
We had nine hammerheads there.

00:03:39.986 --> 00:03:42.255
We got what seemed like
countless nurse sharks.

00:03:44.958 --> 00:03:46.292
What we saw was
that both the nurse

00:03:46.359 --> 00:03:49.662
sharks and the hammerheads
did respond to the magnets.

00:03:49.729 --> 00:03:51.698
So what we can
take away from that

00:03:51.764 --> 00:03:54.133
is that those weak magnetic
fields that are locked

00:03:54.200 --> 00:03:56.369
in volcanic rock are
something that the sharks

00:03:56.436 --> 00:04:00.506
could detect and may be
able to use in navigation.

